category: Mail
requires: cygwin libiconv2 postfix
sdesc: "Heirloom mailx (nail), the mail user agent RHEL ships as /bin/mailx"
ldesc: "Heirloom mailx, formerly known as nail, is a BSD Mail derivative
with MIME, IMAP, POP3, SMTP and S/MIME support. This is the exact program
Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8 ships as the 'mailx' package (upstream 12.5), so it
gives a RHEL-parity /usr/bin/mailx with the 'mail' and 'Mail' aliases. It sends
through any sendmail-compatible MTA; on this replica that is Postfix at
/usr/sbin/sendmail."

